EDICT 0008: WinQuake's version text on the console background of every build

Category: build-independent output, no change in results on Windows.
Draw_ConsoleBackground writes the version into the console picture, chosen by the platform the build is for:
"(WinQuake) 1.09" on Windows, "(Linux Quake 1.30) 1.09" on Linux. With the screen in the hash (-edictscreen),
that made the Linux and Windows references differ in every frame that shows the console. The reference is
WinQuake, so every build takes the Windows text (build.sh defines EDICT). The other build-dependent text on the
screen, the "Exe:" line of Host_Init with __TIME__ and __DATE__, is pinned by build.sh through
SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH, without a patch.

--- a/draw.c
+++ b/draw.c
@@ -548,7 +548,7 @@
 	conback = Draw_CachePic ("gfx/conback.lmp");

 // hack the version number directly into the pic
-#ifdef _WIN32
+#if defined(_WIN32) || defined(EDICT)	// EDICT: WinQuake's text on every build (patch 0008)
 	sprintf (ver, "(WinQuake) %4.2f", (float)VERSION);
 	dest = conback->data + 320*186 + 320 - 11 - 8*strlen(ver);
 #elif defined(X11)
